The '''Lothal system''' was a [[star system]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. It had at least one [[planet]], [[Lothal]]. In the [[Standard year|years]] following the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Galactic Empire]] expanded into the Outer Rim and brought the Lothal system into its territory.<ref name="Spark" /> Lothal became an important world for the [[Imperial Military]], with industries built to serve the creation of the Imperial war machine and [[The galaxy|galactic]] expansion.<ref name="Call to Action">{{Rebels|Call to Action}}</ref> The Empire's presence in the Lothal system led to a [[Spectres|rebel cell]] operating on Lothal, one that struck against numerous Imperial operations in an effort to bring freedom to Lothal and to the galaxy.<ref name="Spark" />

{{System-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Lothal&mdash;and, by extension, the Lothal system&mdash;is the primary setting of the [[Star Wars Rebels Season One|first season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''. The system is not referred to by name in the show until "[[Rebel Resolve]]," the eleventh episode of the first season. Although the system's name is not said at any point in the episode, it is mentioned in [[Aurebesh]] on [[Kanan Jarrus]]' holographic Imperial prisoner file.<ref name="Rebel Resolve">{{Rebels|Rebel Resolve}}</ref>

